  "|The central point of capitalism, as expounded by Karl Marx, is that|capitalists' profit is the surplus value obtained from workers' labour|workers are inherently incapable of being owners of their labour|capitalists shall always increase workers' earning capacity through wages|capitalists shall always readily consent to workers' welfare demands": "ideologies",
  "|A constitution that requires a plebiscite or a referendum to be amended is|rigid|unwritten|flexible|written": "constitution",
